From 13ae66fc343490011372008ee2ddfaac470a20fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HazzPika <188178761+HazzPika@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:26:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 27/29] airoha: en7528: use a raw appended DTB

Device/tclinux-ubi builds the initramfs as "kernel-bin | append-dtb",
which appends a raw DTB to the kernel, but en7528 sets
CONFIG_MIPS_ELF_APPENDED_DTB, which expects the DTB in an ELF section.
RAM-booting such an image panics with "no dtb found". Use
CONFIG_MIPS_RAW_APPENDED_DTB, as OpenWrt's econet target does. Boards
booted through a FIT image (XC220-G3V) still get their DTB from the
bootloader.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 target/linux/airoha/en7528/config-6.18 | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/target/linux/airoha/en7528/config-6.18 b/target/linux/airoha/en7528/config-6.18
index 2b10edeb33..44ec2691d3 100644
--- a/target/linux/airoha/en7528/config-6.18
+++ b/target/linux/airoha/en7528/config-6.18
@@ -154,7 +154,7 @@ CONFIG_MIPS_CPC=y
 CONFIG_MIPS_CPS=y
 # CONFIG_MIPS_CPS_NS16550_BOOL is not set
 CONFIG_MIPS_CPU_SCACHE=y
-CONFIG_MIPS_ELF_APPENDED_DTB=y
+CONFIG_MIPS_RAW_APPENDED_DTB=y
 CONFIG_MIPS_GIC=y
 CONFIG_MIPS_L1_CACHE_SHIFT=5
 CONFIG_MIPS_MT=y
